   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The integrand is a product of x and an exponential, and the derivative of the exponent, \\( 1 \\), does not account for the factor x, so substitution does not apply and the product calls for integration by parts.",
         "rule_named": "technique selected by structure"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Take \\( u = x \\) and \\( dv = e^{x}\\,dx \\), so \\( du = dx \\) and \\( v = e^{x} \\). Then the integral is \\( x e^{x} - \\int e^{x}\\,dx \\).",
         "rule_named": "integration by parts"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Antidifferentiate the remaining exponential: the integral is \\( x e^{x} - e^{x} + C \\).",
